=== SURVEY ===
Web source SkipToContent.tsx (components/feedback) is the WCAG 2.4.1 (Bypass Blocks, Level A) skip
link. It composes `<VisuallyHidden as="a" focusable href="#main-content">` — visually hidden until
focused, then a fixed ringed pill via `focus:*` utilities — and on activation `e.preventDefault()`,
`document.getElementById('main-content').focus({preventScroll:false})` +
`main.scrollIntoView({block:'start'})`, so keyboard / assistive-technology users skip past the
50+ sidebar items to the body. It MUST be the first interactive element in the DOM.
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (the only hook). Shared components: @/components/a11y
(VisuallyHidden). Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys extracted from source: exactly ONE — `a11y.skipToContent` (default "Skip to main content").
Existing native: an ATOMIC `TSSkipToContent` already lives in Sources/Components/Feedback/States.swift
(the component-library bundle, which this prompt lists Out of Scope). NO Skip* surface symbols exist
(SkipToContent/SkipTarget/SkipConnection/SkipLandmarkRegistry/SkipFocusing/… are collision-free).
`AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(_).post()` already used in-repo (AnnouncerRegion.Seams,
AchievementUnlockListener, WidgetPicker, AppShell) → the native bypass-blocks voicing API is valid.
Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/AnnouncerRegion (the sibling a11y surface 0001 —
Adapter/Model/Seams/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests/ModelTests).

=== REASONING ===
- The web component renders one sr-only anchor; the prompt requires a production-polished native
  surface reproducing its DATA, composition, states and (native-chrome) i18n, with EVERY state
  visible (no blank box). Chosen, mirroring the accepted AnnouncerRegion precedent: a native
  skip-navigation panel — the hero "Skip to main content" link (the verbatim web string) over any
  secondary registered landmarks — that performs the REAL focus move through a coordinator seam
  (AccessibilityNotification + a host-wired @AccessibilityFocusState), so the bypass-blocks contract
  is reproduced, not just drawn.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical AnnouncerRegion leaf:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): SkipResolve i18n seam; SkipTarget (id=anchor id, label, isPrimary);
    SkipAnchor (verbatim port of href="#main-content" ⇄ getElementById('main-content'));
    SkipToContentAccessibility (namedSkipLabel / skipConfirmation builders).
  • Model: SkipToContentTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; SkipConnection axis;
    SkipToContentInput snapshot (derives primary = first isPrimary else first, the web #main-content
    selection, + ordered secondary); Resolved + Projection (error/loading/empty/data); @Observable
    SkipToContentModel (binds source, routes skip() to the focuser, one-shot stale auto-refresh);
    SkipToContentStrings i18n facade (table "SkipToContent").
  • Seams: SkipFocusing seam (native parity of main.focus()+scrollIntoView) + OSLog default +
    AccessibilitySkipFocuser (posts a real AccessibilityNotification.Announcement + invokes the host
    focus hook); SkipToContentSource protocol; SkipLandmarkRegistry (the native port of the
    #main-content element living in the DOM — register/unregister/subscribe/reset, upsert-by-id
    preserving first-seen order) + SkipLandmarkSubscription; LiveSkipToContentSource (bridges the
    registry into snapshots); InMemorySkipToContentSource (previews/tests).
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- States rendered: loading (skeleton skip-link rows), empty (no landmark registered — friendly
  TSEmptyState, never blank), error (retry — web QueryError peer), data (hero link + secondary
  links + bypass-blocks explainer), and the orthogonal connection axis stale/offline (freshness chip
  + one-shot auto-refresh on the stale transition).
- The hero link reveals an accent focus ring via @FocusState (the native parity of the web
  `focus:ring-2` reveal); on touch it is always present and reachable first (the web "first
  interactive element" intent). The primary link text is the verbatim web `a11y.skipToContent`.
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/sr-only literally (native has no aria sr-only-until-focus — used
  @FocusState reveal + the platform AccessibilityNotification, the idiomatic equivalents); a truly
  invisible surface (the P4 leaf contract forbids blank boxes — rendered the skip links visibly as a
  panel); direct focus posting from the view (routed through the SkipFocusing seam so it is
  unit-testable); HTTP in the view (bound via the source seam).
- The pre-existing atomic TSSkipToContent (component-library bundle) is left untouched (Out of Scope);
  this surface is the full shared-surface, name-distinct (SkipToContent vs TSSkipToContent).

